1582 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (The Fragile Five was a name invented in August 2013 by a banking analyst, James Lord, to describe Brazil, India, Indonesia, South Africa and Turkey. These emerging economies accounted for 12% of global GDP and 20% of global economic growth between 2009 and 2013. They had, however, a heavy reliance on external finance and were seen as the most susceptible to sudden changes in the direction of hot money flows. In early 2014 they had large current account deficits, slowing economic growth, inflation rates between 6% and 11% and were generally experiencing falling exchange rates.)
/E (The Fragile Five was a name invented in August 2013 by a banking analyst, James Lord, to describe Brazil, India, Indonesia, South Africa and Turkey. These emerging economies accounted for 12% of global GDP and 20% of global economic growth between 2009 and 2013. They had, however, a heavy reliance on external finance and were seen as the most susceptible to sudden changes in the direction of hot money flows. In early 2014 they had large current account deficits, slowing economic growth, inflation rates between 6% and 11% and were generally experiencing falling exchange rates.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
