/T (Such actions have reignited the debate surrounding the benefits of protectionism. Whilst some EU anti-dumping measures have already been implemented in the steel industry, it is argued that further tariffs might be necessary to protect British jobs. However, the Chinese government says this goes against the terms of the agreement it reached when it joined the World Trade Organisation in 2001. Indeed, this is just one of many trade disputes which have occurred between China and the EU in recent years.)
